### Wasteland Multiball / Loot: {heading--wasteland}

Completing the nuke standup targets on the right side of the playfield will light the left ramp to load the Fat Man nuke launcher and kill an enemy. The player can loot enemies for goods by shooting the right scoop after defeating one. Defeating all three enemies will start Wasteland Multiball.

*Pro*: Enemies are killed every time the lit left ramp is made.
*Prem / LE*: The player must use the flippers and action button to rotate the nuke launcher and kill an enemy on the upper playfield. If the player has filled up VATS with enough switch hits, the player will be guaranteed to strike down an enemy on the next shot.

During Wasteland Multiball, score jackpots at the lit shots to light a super jackpot that can be earned by shooting the left ramp and using the Fat Man launcher to fire at the middle nuke standup target. The process then repeats with more jackpots required to light super jackpot.

## Other Scoring: {heading--otherfeatures}

### Power Armor (2x Playfield): {heading--playfieldx}

Hit the bumper near the junk target to increase the fusion core power. Holding, then releasing the action button while the player has enough fusion core power will activate 2x scoring for the duration of the time shown on the gauge near the left flipper. The player can turn off the power armor if they want to preserve it by holding the action button again.

### Junk / Score Multiplier: {heading--junk}

Collecting junk by shooting shots around the playfield, including the left target where the left slingshot would usually be, will allow the player to create new weapons at thresholds of 5 junk found. Every new weapon constructed increases the global scoring multiplier for the game by +0.2x. The multiplier caps at 2x.

### Radroaches / Radaway Hurry-Up: {heading--radroach}

Hitting the lit green standup targets scattered around the playfield will kill Radroaches and deal radiation damage that lowers the player's maximum HP amount. However, they will also light Radaway hurry-ups at random shots that will restore health and increase the Radaway jackpot. After scoring enough hurry-ups, shoot all three ramps to light the Radaway jackpot for collection at the upper loop.

Kill enough Radroaches to light **[extra ball](#heading--extraballs)**.

### Companions: {heading--companions}

Shoot the yellow shots around the playfield to qualify companions that can be used by short pressing the action button. 

* **Mr. Handy**: Spots a **[Deathclaw](#heading--deathclaw)** shot. Easier to boost **[fusion core](#heading--playfieldx)** power.
* **Protectron**: Spots all lit **[Radaway awards](#heading--radroach)**. Boost **[quest timers](#heading--mainquests)**.
* **Dogmeat**: Collects all lit **[junk](#heading--junk)**. Lights more **[radroaches](#heading--radroach)** to kill.

### Cap Stash / Spinner: {heading--caps}

Complete the left and right inlanes to lower the center spinner for a cap stash rip. Every spin adds caps that can be used to purchase items from **[sundries](#heading--shop)**.

### Sundries (Shop): {heading--shop}

Once the player has enough **[caps](#heading--caps}, shooting the right scoop will allow them to purchase items from the shop. 

If the player wants an item but doesn't have the caps to purchase it, they can attempt to steal the item from the shop. If they do, they must shoot the right ramp within 10 seconds to escape with the item, and all items will cost double the amount they were before the next time they visit the shop.

### Stimpaks (Outlane Ball Save): {heading--stimpaks}

Earn stimpaks by making shots lit with white stimpak inserts. Stimpaks prevent the ball from draining down an outlane by relaunching them into play.

With strong enough **[perception](#heading--special)**, the player can use the flippers to lane-change the lit stimpaks between outlanes.

